urface (μ = 0.25). The horizontal force needed to move it at constant speed is (g = 10 m/s²)", "10 N", "40 N", "4 N", "25 N", "F = μmg = 0.25 × 4 × 10 = 10 N."], ["Physics", "", "A bullet of mass 20 g travelling at 400 m/s embeds in a 3.98 kg block hanging from a string. The speed of the block + bullet immediately after is", "2 m/s", "4 m/s", "1 m/s", "100 m/s", "0.02 × 400 = 4.0 × v → v = 2 m/s."], ["Physics", "", "The block in the previous question rises to a maximum height of (g = 10 m/s²)", "0.2 m", "0.4 m", "2 m", "0.1 m", "h = v²/2g = 4/20 = 0.2 m."], ["Physics", "", "A girl whirls a 0.5 kg stone on a string 0.8 m long in a horizontal circle at 4 m/s. The tension is", "10 N", "5 N", "20 N", "40 N", "T = mv²/r = 0.5 × 16/0.8 = 10 N."], ["Physics", "", "A 60 W lamp operates from a 240 V supply. The current is", "0.25 A", "4 A", "0.5 A", "14.4 A", "I = P/V = 60/240 = 0.25 A."], ["Physics", "", "A heater of resistance 48 Ω is connected to a 240 V supply. The power is", "1 200 W", "5 W", "11 520 W", "240 W", "P = V²/R = 57 600/48 = 1 200 W."], ["Physics", "", "A potentiometer wire is 100 cm long. A cell balances at 62 cm. If the driver voltage is 2 V, the e.m.f. of the cell is", "1.24 V", "0.62 V", "3.2 V", "1.62 V", "E = (62/100) × 2 = 1.24 V."], ["Physics", "", "A moving-coil galvanometer of resistance 50 Ω gives full-scale deflection for 2 mA. To convert it to a voltmeter reading 10 V, the series resistance needed is", "4 950 Ω", "5 000 Ω", "50 Ω", "950 Ω", "R = V/I − Rg = 5 000 − 50 = 4 950 Ω."], ["Physics", "", "The same galvanometer (50 Ω, 2 mA) is converted to an ammeter reading 1 A. The shunt resistance is approximately", "0.1 Ω", "50 Ω", "0.5 Ω", "2 Ω", "Rs = Ig·Rg/(I − Ig) = 0.002 × 50/0.998 ≈ 0.1 Ω."], ["Physics", "", "Two long parallel wires carry currents of 5 A and 10 A in the same direction, 0.1 m apart. The force per metre between them is (μ₀ = 4π×10⁻⁷)", "1 × 10⁻⁴ N/m attractive", "1 × 10⁻⁴ N/m repulsive", "2 × 10⁻⁴ N/m attractive", "5 × 10⁻5 N/m repulsive", "F/L = μ₀I₁I₂/2πd = 2×10⁻⁷ × 50/0.1 = 1×10⁻⁴ N/m; currents in the same direction attract."], ["Physics", "", "A solenoid with 2 000 turns per metre carries 3 A. The magnetic flux density inside is (μ₀ = 4π×10⁻⁷)", "7.5 × 10⁻³ T", "2.4 × 10⁻⁴ T", "1.2 × 10⁻³ T", "0.24 T", "B = μ₀nI = 4π×10⁻⁷ × 2000 × 3 ≈ 7.5 × 10⁻³ T."], ["Physics", "", "A rod 0.5 m long moves at 4 m/s perpendicular to a field of 0.2 T. The induced e.m.f. is", "0.4 V", "0.8 V", "0.04 V", "4 V", "e = Blv = 0.2 × 0.5 × 4 = 0.4 V."], ["Physics", "", "An RLC series circuit has R = 30 Ω, X_L = 70 Ω and X_C = 30 Ω at 50 Hz. The impedance is", "50 Ω", "70 Ω", "130 Ω", "30 Ω", "Z = √(30² + (70 − 30)²) = √(900 + 1 600) = 50 Ω."], ["Physics", "", "The resonant frequency of a series circuit with L = 1 H and C = 100 μF is approximately", "15.9 Hz", "159 Hz", "1.59 Hz", "50 Hz", "f = 1/(2π√LC) = 1/(2π × 0.01) = 15.9 Hz."], ["Physics", "", "A step-up transformer with 100 primary turns and 1 000 secondary turns is 90% efficient. Input power is 500 W at 20 V. The output current is", "0.225 A", "2.25 A", "0.5 A", "22.5 A", "Output power = 450 W; Vs = 200 V; I = 450/200 = 2.25 A."], ["Physics", "", "The de Broglie wavelength of an electron moving at 2 × 10⁶ m/s is (h = 6.6×10⁻³⁴, m = 9.1×10⁻³¹)", "3.6 × 10⁻¹⁰ m", "3.6 × 10⁻⁷ m", "7.3 × 10⁻¹⁰ m", "1.2 × 10⁻¹⁷ m", "λ = h/mv = 6.6×10⁻³⁴ / (9.1×10⁻³¹ × 2×10⁶) = 3.6 × 10⁻¹⁰ m."], ["Physics", "", "An excited hydrogen atom drops from the energy level −1.51 eV to −3.40 eV. The wavelength of light emitted is (hc = 1240 eV nm)", "656 nm", "1 240 nm", "328 nm", "410 nm", "ΔE = 1.89 eV; λ = 1240/1.89 ≈ 656 nm."], ["Physics", "", "The activity of a source falls from 1 600 Bq to 100 Bq in 12 hours. The half-life is", "3 hours", "6 hours", "2 hours", "4 hours", "1 600 → 100 is 4 half-lives, so t½ = 12/4 = 3 hours."], ["Physics", "", "The decay constant of a nucleus with half-life 10 s is (ln 2 = 0.693)", "0.0693 s⁻¹", "6.93 s⁻¹", "0.693 s⁻¹", "0.0069 s⁻¹", "λ = 0.693/10."], ["Physics", "", "An ideal gas at 300 K and pressure P is heated at constant volume until the pressure is 2P. The temperature is", "600 K", "150 K", "327 K", "900 K", "P/T constant."], ["Physics", "", "The internal energy of 1 mol of a monatomic ideal gas at 300 K is (R = 8.3 J/mol K)", "3 735 J", "2 490 J", "6 225 J", "1 245 J", "U = 3/2 RT = 1.5 × 8.3 × 300 = 3 735 J."], ["Physics", "", "A Carnot engine works between 500 K and 300 K. Its efficiency is", "40%", "60%", "20%", "83%", "1 − 300/500 = 0.4."], ["Physics", "", "A refrigerator takes 200 J from the cold space using 50 J of work. Its coefficient of performance is", "4", "0.25", "5", "1.25", "COP = Q_c/W = 200/50 = 4."], ["Physics", "", "Heat flows through a wall of area 10 m², thickness 0.2 m and conductivity 0.8 W/m K with a temperature difference of 10 K. The rate of heat flow is", "400 W", "16 W", "80 W", "160 W", "P = kAΔT/d = 0.8×10×10/0.2 = 400 W."], ["Physics", "", "A black body at 600 K radiates at a rate proportional to T⁴. If its temperature is doubled, the rate increases by a factor of", "16", "4", "8", "2", "(2)⁴ = 16."], ["Physics", "", "A sound has intensity 10⁻⁶ W/m². Taking the threshold 10⁻¹² W/m², the intensity level is", "60 dB", "6 dB", "120 dB", "12 dB", "10 log(10⁶) = 60 dB."], ["Physics", "", "An organ pipe open at both ends has a fundamental frequency of 340 Hz (v = 340 m/s). Its length is", "0.5 m", "1.0 m", "0.25 m", "2.0 m", "L = v/2f = 340/680 = 0.5 m."], ["Physics", "", "A train sounding a horn of 400 Hz moves away from a stationary observer at 20 m/s (v = 340 m/s). The observed frequency is", "378 Hz", "425 Hz", "400 Hz", "350 Hz", "f' = 400 × 340/360 = 377.8 Hz."], ["Physics", "", "A water wave with wavelength 4 m and period 2 s has speed", "2 m/s", "8 m/s", "0.5 m/s", "6 m/s", "v = λ/T = 2 m/s."], ["Physics", "", "A lens of power +5 D is combined in contact with a lens of power −2 D. The focal length of the combination is", "33.3 cm", "20 cm", "14.3 cm", "50 cm", "P = 3 D, f = 1/3 m = 33.3 cm."], ["Physics", "", "An object is 15 cm from a concave mirror of focal length 10 cm. The image distance is", "30 cm", "6 cm", "25 cm", "10 cm", "1/v = 1/10 − 1/15 = 1/30."], ["Physics", "", "A ray of light enters a glass block (n = 1.5) at 45° to the normal. sin r =", "0.47", "0.67", "0.71", "1.06", "sin r = sin 45°/1.5 = 0.707/1.5 = 0.47."], ["Physics", "", "The angular magnification of a telescope with an objective of focal length 120 cm and an eyepiece of focal length 4 cm is", "30", "480", "124", "0.033", "M = f₀/fₑ = 30."], ["Physics", "", "The thickness measured by a micrometer reads 3.56 mm with a zero error of +0.02 mm. The true thickness is", "3.54 mm", "3.58 mm", "3.56 mm", "3.52 mm", "Corrected = reading − zero error."], ["Physics", "", "In an experiment, the mass is 20.0 ± 0.2 g and the volume 8.0 ± 0.2 cm³. The percentage uncertainty in density is", "3.5%", "1%", "0.4%", "2.5%", "1% + 2.5% = 3.5%."], ["Physics", "", "The slope of a graph of T² against L for a simple pendulum is 4 s²/m. The value of g is (T² = 4π²L/g)", "9.87 m/s²", "4 m/s²", "39.5 m/s²", "1.0 m/s²", "g = 4π²/slope = 39.48/4 = 9.87 m/s²."], ["Physics", "", "A car's engine delivers 60 kW. At a steady speed of 30 m/s the resistive force is", "2 000 N", "1 800 N", "200 N", "60 000 N", "F = P/v = 2 000 N."], ["Chemistry", "", "The mass of 2.5 mol of Na₂CO₃ is (Na = 23, C = 12, O = 16)", "265 g", "106 g", "212 g", "132.5 g", "M = 106 g/mol; 2.5 × 106 = 265 g."], ["Chemistry", "", "The number of atoms in 0.25 mol of ammonia, NH₃, is (L = 6 × 10²³)", "6 × 10²³", "1.5 × 10²³", "3 × 10²³", "2.4 × 10²⁴", "0.25 mol of molecules × 4 atoms each = 1 mol of atoms = 6 × 10²³."], ["Chemistry", "", "The percentage by mass of sulphur in sulphur trioxide, SO₃, is (S = 32, O = 16)", "40%", "50%", "60%", "32%", "32/80 = 40%."], ["Chemistry", "", "A compound contains 40% C, 6.7% H and 53.3% O and has a molar mass of 180. Its molecular formula is", "C₆H₁₂O₆", "CH₂O", "C₃H₆O₃", "C₆H₆O₆", "Empirical CH₂O = 30; 180/30 = 6, so C₆H₁₂O₆."], ["Chemistry", "", "The volume of oxygen at s.t.p. needed for the complete combustion of 5.8 g of butane, C₄H₁₀, is (C = 12, H = 1; 2C₄H₁₀ + 13O₂ → 8CO₂ + 10H₂O)", "14.56 dm³", "11.2 dm³", "22.4 dm³", "7.28 dm³", "n(butane) = 0.1 mol; O₂ = 0.65 mol; V = 0.65 × 22.4 = 14.56 dm³."], ["Chemistry", "", "A 0.5 g sample of impure Na₂CO₃ requires 40.0 cm³ of 0.20 mol dm⁻³ HCl for complete reaction (Na₂CO₃ + 2HCl → 2NaCl + H₂O + CO₂). The percentage purity is (Na₂CO₃ = 106)", "84.8%", "42.4%", "50%", "100%", "n(HCl) = 0.008; n(Na₂CO₃) = 0.004 mol = 0.424 g; 0.424/0.5 = 84.8%."], ["Chemistry", "", "What volume of 0.10 mol dm⁻³ NaOH is needed to neutralise 20 cm³ of 0.15 mol dm⁻³ H₃PO₄ to form Na₃PO₄?", "90 cm³", "30 cm³", "60 cm³", "20 cm³", "n(H₃PO₄) = 0.003; ×3 = 0.009 mol NaOH; V = 0.009/0.10 = 90 cm³."], ["Chemistry", "", "The solubility of a salt is 12 g per 100 g of water at 20 °C. The mass of salt in 280 g of a saturated solution is", "30 g", "12 g", "33.6 g", "24 g", "112 g of solution contains 12 g salt; 280/112 × 12 = 30 g."], ["Chemistry", "", "For the equilibrium PCl₅ ⇌ PCl₃ + Cl₂, the equilibrium concentrations are 0.2, 0.1 and 0.1 mol dm⁻³ respectively. Kc is", "0.05 mol dm⁻³", "0.5 mol dm⁻³", "0.02 mol dm⁻³", "5 mol dm⁻³", "Kc = (0.1 × 0.1)/0.2 = 0.05."], ["Chemistry", "", "For 2SO₂ + O₂ ⇌ 2SO₃, Kc = 4 at a certain temperature. If [SO₂] = 0.5 and [O₂] = 1.0 mol dm⁻³, [SO₃] is", "1.0 mol dm⁻³", "0.25 mol dm⁻³", "2.0 mol dm⁻³", "0.5 mol dm⁻³", "[SO₃]² = 4 × 0.25 × 1.0 = 1.0, so [SO₃] = 1.0."], ["Chemistry", "", "The pH of 0.05 mol dm⁻³ Ba(OH)₂ solution is", "13.0", "12.7", "13.3", "12.0", "[OH⁻] = 0.1; pOH = 1; pH = 13."], ["Chemistry", "", "The pH of a buffer containing 0.1 mol dm⁻³ ethanoic acid and 0.1 mol dm⁻³ sodium ethanoate (Kₐ = 1.8 × 10⁻⁵) is", "4.74", "3.74", "5.74", "7.0", "pH = pKa + log(1) = 4.74."], ["Chemistry", "", "When 100 cm³ of 1.0 mol dm⁻³ HCl is mixed with 100 cm³ of 1.0 mol dm⁻³ NaOH, the temperature rises by 6.8 °C. (c = 4.2 J g⁻¹ K⁻¹, mass 200 g.) The enthalpy of neutralisation per mole is approximately", "−57 kJ mol⁻¹", "−5.7 kJ mol⁻¹", "−114 kJ mol⁻¹", "−28.5 kJ mol⁻¹", "Q = 200 × 4.2 × 6.8 = 5 712 J for 0.1 mol → 57 kJ/mol."], ["Chemistry", "", "The standard enthalpies of formation of CH₄(g), CO₂(g) and H₂O(l) are −75, −394 and −286 kJ mol⁻¹. The enthalpy of combustion of methane is", "−891 kJ mol⁻¹", "−605 kJ mol⁻¹", "+891 kJ mol⁻¹", "−1 056 kJ mol⁻¹", "−394 + 2(−286) − (−75) = −891."], ["Chemistry", "", "Bond energies: C–H 413, O=O 498, C=O 805, O–H 464 (kJ/mol). For CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O(g), ΔH is approximately", "−818 kJ mol⁻¹", "+818 kJ mol⁻¹", "−1 636 kJ mol⁻¹", "−409 kJ mol⁻¹", "Bonds broken: 4(413) + 2(498) = 2 648; formed: 2(805) + 4(464) = 3 466; ΔH = 2 648 − 3 466 = −818."], ["Chemistry", "", "A first-order reaction has a rate constant of 3.5 × 10⁻³ s⁻¹. Its half-life is (ln 2 = 0.693)", "198 s", "2.4 s", "350 s", "0.0024 s", "t½ = 0.693/3.5×10⁻³ = 198 s."], ["Chemistry", "", "If the rate of a reaction doubles for every 10 °C rise in temperature, by what factor does it increase from 25 °C to 55 °C?", "8", "6", "3", "16", "Three 10 °C steps: 2³ = 8."], ["Chemistry", "", "Using the data: Eₐ lowered by a catalyst from 80 to 60 kJ mol⁻¹, ΔH is", "unchanged", "lowered by 20 kJ", "raised by 20 kJ", "zero", "A catalyst does not change ΔH."], ["Chemistry", "", "A cell is set up with a standard hydrogen electrode and a Zn²⁺/Zn electrode (E° = −0.76 V). The zinc electrode is the", "negative terminal (anode)", "positive terminal", "salt bridge", "cathode", "Zinc is oxidised and supplies electrons."], ["Chemistry", "", "The quantity of electricity needed to deposit 1 mol of aluminium from Al³⁺ is", "3 F", "1 F", "2 F", "6 F", "Al³⁺ + 3e⁻ → Al."], ["Chemistry", "", "The mass of aluminium deposited by 9 650 C is (Al = 27, F = 96 500 C)", "0.9 g", "2.7 g", "0.3 g", "9 g", "n(e⁻) = 0.1 mol; n(Al) = 0.1/3 mol; mass = 0.9 g."], ["Chemistry", "", "In the electrolysis of brine in a diaphragm cell, the products are", "chlorine, hydrogen and sodium hydroxide", "sodium and chlorine", "oxygen and hydrogen", "sodium and oxygen", "Cl⁻ is oxidised, water is reduced, leaving NaOH."], ["Chemistry", "", "Which species is the strongest reducing agent? (E°: Li⁺/Li = −3.04 V, Zn²⁺/Zn = −0.76 V, Cu²⁺/Cu = +0.34 V, Ag⁺/Ag = +0.80 V)", "Li", "Zn", "Cu", "Ag", "The most negative E° means the strongest reducing agent."], ["Chemistry", "", "The IUPAC name of CH₃CH₂CH(CH₃)CH(CH₃)CH₃ is", "2,3-dimethylpentane", "3,4-dimethylpentane", "2-ethyl-3-methylbutane", "hexane", "Longest chain 5 C; methyls on carbons 2 and 3."], ["Chemistry", "", "The number of possible alkenes with formula C₄H₈ (including geometric isomers) is", "4", "2", "3", "5", "But-1-ene, cis- and trans-but-2-ene, 2-methylpropene."], ["Chemistry", "", "The test that distinguishes propan-2-ol from propan-1-ol uses", "oxidation with acidified dichromate, followed by Tollens’ test on the product", "litmus paper", "sodium metal", "bromine water", "The primary alcohol gives an aldehyde (silver mirror); the secondary gives a ketone (none)."], ["Chemistry", "", "The reaction of ethanoyl chloride with ethanol gives", "ethyl ethanoate", "ethanoic acid", "ethanal", "diethyl ether", "Acyl chlorides esterify alcohols."], ["Chemistry", "", "The product of reducing ethanal with LiAlH₄ is", "ethanol", "ethanoic acid", "ethane", "ethene", "The carbonyl group becomes an alcohol."], ["Chemistry", "", "Aniline (phenylamine) is made by reducing", "nitrobenzene", "benzoic acid", "phenol", "benzaldehyde", "Tin and HCl reduce the nitro group."], ["Chemistry", "", "The type of reaction in the conversion of ethene to ethane using nickel is", "addition (reduction)", "substitution", "elimination", "condensation", "Hydrogenation adds across the C=C bond."], ["Chemistry", "", "A polypeptide is formed by", "condensation of amino acids", "addition of alkenes", "esterification of alcohols", "hydrolysis of fats", "Peptide bonds form with loss of water."], ["Chemistry", "", "The monomer of PVC is", "chloroethene", "ethene", "tetrafluoroethene", "propene", "Poly(chloroethene)."], ["Chemistry", "", "The enzyme zymase converts glucose into", "ethanol and carbon dioxide", "lactic acid", "starch", "glycerol", "Fermentation by yeast."], ["Chemistry", "", "Which of the following is a reducing sugar?", "glucose", "sucrose", "starch", "cellulose", "It has a free aldehyde group."], ["Chemistry", "", "Adding bromine water to phenol gives", "a white precipitate of 2,4,6-tribromophenol", "no reaction", "a blue solution", "a yellow gas", "The ring is strongly activated."], ["Chemistry", "", "The gas produced when concentrated H₂SO₄ is added to sodium chloride is", "hydrogen chloride", "chlorine", "sulphur dioxide", "oxygen", "A displacement of the volatile acid."], ["Chemistry", "", "Hard water can be softened by adding", "sodium carbonate", "calcium chloride", "sodium chloride", "dilute acid", "Carbonate precipitates Ca²⁺ and Mg²⁺."], ["Chemistry", "", "The oxide of nitrogen formed in car engines that contributes to acid rain is", "NO₂", "N₂O", "NH₃", "N₂", "It forms nitric acid in water."], ["Chemistry", "", "The ore from which zinc is mainly obtained is", "zinc blende (ZnS)", "bauxite", "haematite", "cassiterite", "Roasted in air to give ZnO."], ["Chemistry", "", "The percentage of nitrogen by mass in urea, CO(NH₂)₂, is (N = 14, C = 12, O = 16, H = 1)", "46.7%", "23.3%", "28%", "14%", "M = 60; N = 28; 28/60 = 46.7%."], ["Biology", "", "A cross between a pure-breeding tall plant (TT) and a dwarf plant (tt) gives an F₁ that is self-pollinated. The F₂ ratio of tall to dwarf is", "3 : 1", "1 : 1", "1 : 2 : 1", "9 : 3 : 3 : 1", "F₁ is Tt; Tt × Tt gives 3 tall : 1 dwarf."], ["Biology", "", "Incomplete dominance in snapdragons (red × white → pink) gives, in the F₂,", "1 red : 2 pink : 1 white", "3 red : 1 white", "all pink", "1 red : 1 white", "Heterozygotes show an intermediate phenotype."]